From 06f2010b9e574a4eba81baf33b6412aa52228080 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 21 Jun 2026 08:58:36 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 03223/11362] [outer-loop] fix _delta cap=80 bug: lossless RLE
 for world-model induction evidence

BUG: _transitions_block fed the induce prompt _delta(...,cap=80) -- truncating every transition
to the first 80 changed cells. Games with large per-action re-renders (e.g. a 293-cell change)
showed the model only 27% of what the action did, starving rule-induction. Affects all
un-adaptered games using the E3 LLM-induction tier.

FIX: _rle_delta() -- lossless run-length encoding 'r<row>c<col>:<v0,v1,...>' (comma-separated so
colors >=10 are unambiguous). Shows the FULL change at ~1/6 the chars of raw per-cell tuples, so
the complete change fits the model's context WITHOUT truncation (the new full prompt is actually
smaller than the old truncated one). Prompt description updated to parse runs. _delta kept (still
used for the verifier's deliberately-capped illustrative mismatch examples); arc_gap_fill's hard
cap is intentional (heuristic prompts need game-sense, not full dynamics) and unchanged.

Verified lossless 300/300 incl. colors 0-15; 42 existing e3 induction tests pass; new regression
test test_rle_delta_lossless.py (3 scenarios). Partial commit; conductor in-flight untouched.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
